From: Pratyush Singhal <pratyush.singhal@scale.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Apr 2026 18:17:25 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Add Docker build infrastructure for OpenClaw base image

Dockerfile and build-and-push.sh for building a base image with the forked
OpenClaw gateway, system dependencies, Chromium, and all channel extensions.

Build notes:
- Excludes only extensions/tlon (broken @tloncorp/api TypeScript errors)
- All other channels included (telegram, whatsapp, discord, slack, etc.)
- Includes make/g++/python3 for native addon builds

Usage:
  ./docker/build-and-push.sh         # tag: openclaw-2026.3.2-v0.0.1
  ./docker/build-and-push.sh v0.0.2  # tag: openclaw-2026.3.2-v0.0.2

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 docker/Dockerfile        | 52 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 docker/build-and-push.sh | 39 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 91 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 docker/Dockerfile
 create mode 100755 docker/build-and-push.sh

diff --git a/docker/Dockerfile b/docker/Dockerfile
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..2a19429e26
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docker/Dockerfile
@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+# OpenClaw Base Image
+#
+# Provides the OpenClaw gateway runtime (with tool.execute RPC support),
+# system dependencies, and Chromium for headless browser automation.
+#
+# This image is used as the base for Scale's openclaw-environment image,
+# which adds entrypoint scripts, skills, personas, and other config.
+#
+# Build & push:
+#   ./docker/build-and-push.sh [tag]
+
+FROM node:22-slim AS builder
+
+RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y git python3 make g++ && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*
+RUN corepack enable && corepack prepare pnpm@10.23.0 --activate
+
+COPY . /build
+WORKDIR /build
+
+# The tlon extension's git-hosted dep (@tloncorp/api) has TypeScript
+# compilation errors at the pinned commit — exclude only tlon, keep all
+# other channel extensions (telegram, whatsapp, discord, slack, etc.).
+RUN rm -rf extensions/tlon
+
+RUN pnpm install && pnpm build && pnpm pack
+
+# ── Runtime image ──
+FROM node:22-slim
+
+# Core utilities + Chromium for headless browser automation
+RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y \
+    curl git python3-pip \
+    ffmpeg \
+    chromium \
+    fonts-liberation fonts-noto-color-emoji \
+    libatk-bridge2.0-0 libatk1.0-0 libcups2 libdbus-1-3 \
+    libdrm2 libgbm1 libgtk-3-0 libnspr4 libnss3 \
+    libxcomposite1 libxdamage1 libxrandr2 xdg-utils \
+    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*
+
+# Tell OpenClaw / Playwright where to find the browser
+ENV CHROME_PATH="/usr/bin/chromium"
+
+# Install OpenClaw from the build stage + mcporter (MCP server/tool CLI)
+COPY --from=builder /build/openclaw-*.tgz /tmp/openclaw.tgz
+RUN npm install -g /tmp/openclaw.tgz mcporter@latest && rm -f /tmp/openclaw.tgz
+
+# Create standard OpenClaw directories
+RUN mkdir -p /root/.openclaw \
+             /root/.openclaw/agents/main/sessions \
+             /root/.openclaw/credentials \
+             /workspace /traces
diff --git a/docker/build-and-push.sh b/docker/build-and-push.sh
new file mode 100755
index 0000000000..b71cdc088e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docker/build-and-push.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+#!/bin/bash
+set -euo pipefail
+
+# Build and push the OpenClaw base image to ECR.
+#
+# Usage:
+#   ./docker/build-and-push.sh              # uses default tag
+#   ./docker/build-and-push.sh v0.0.2       # custom version suffix
+#
+# Prerequisites:
+#   - Docker CLI (or Rancher Desktop)
+#   - AWS ECR login: aws ecr get-login-password --region us-west-2 | \
+#       docker login --username AWS --password-stdin 307185671274.dkr.ecr.us-west-2.amazonaws.com
+
+ECR_REPO="307185671274.dkr.ecr.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/openclaw-environment"
+OPENCLAW_VERSION="2026.3.2"
+VERSION_SUFFIX="${1:-v0.0.1}"
+TAG="openclaw-${OPENCLAW_VERSION}-${VERSION_SUFFIX}"
+FULL_TAG="${ECR_REPO}:${TAG}"
+
+SCRIPT_DIR="$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)"
+REPO_ROOT="$(cd "${SCRIPT_DIR}/.." && pwd)"
+
+echo "Building OpenClaw base image..."
+echo "  Tag: ${FULL_TAG}"
+echo "  Context: ${REPO_ROOT}"
+
+docker buildx build \
+  --platform linux/amd64 \
+  -f "${SCRIPT_DIR}/Dockerfile" \
+  -t "${FULL_TAG}" \
+  --push \
+  "${REPO_ROOT}"
+
+echo ""
+echo "Pushed: ${FULL_TAG}"
+echo ""
+echo "To use in Scale's Dockerfile:"
+echo "  FROM ${FULL_TAG}"
